{
  "info": {
    "name": "Agent Platform API",
    "_postman_id": "a1e7c0de-0001-4a00-9a00-agentplatform01",
    "description": "Runnable collection for the agent-platform server (NestJS, default http://localhost:4100).\n\n## Authentication\nEvery endpoint except `GET /health` is signed. A **collection-level pre-request script** adds these headers automatically on each send:\n- `X-Operator-Id` — the operator id (collection variable `operatorId`)\n- `X-Api-Key` — the operator api key (`apiKey`)\n- `X-Timestamp` — unix seconds, must be within ±5 minutes of the server clock\n- `X-Signature` — `hex( HMAC-SHA256(signingSecret, \"<timestamp>.<rawBody>\") )`\n\nYou do **not** add the `x-*` headers yourself. Just set the four credential variables (below) and send.\n\n## Variables (Collection tab → Variables)\n| Variable | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `baseUrl` | http://localhost:4100 | Server base URL |\n| `operatorId` | demo-operator | From `npm run seed` |\n| `apiKey` | demo-api-key | From `npm run seed` |\n| `signingSecret` | demo-signing-secret | From `npm run seed` (secret) |\n| `managerUsername` | mgr1 | Username for the created agent |\n| `createKey` / `creditKey` / `withdrawKey` | k-* | Idempotency-Key per money move |\n| `agentId` | (auto) | Set by the **Create agent** test from its response |\n| `weekId` | 2026-W44 | Weekly-close id |\n\n## Run order\n1. **Health** (open, no auth)\n2. **Agents → Create top-level agent** — captures `agentId` for the rest\n3. **Credit → Grant / Withdraw**\n4. **Events**, **Weeks → Closing**\n5. **Negative tests** — expected 401 / 400 / 422\n\nUse the Collection Runner to run them all in sequence.\n\n## Idempotency\nMoney moves require an `Idempotency-Key` header. Re-sending the same key with the same body **replays the first result** (no double credit, same agent) — that is by design. Change the key variable to perform a genuinely new move.\n\n## Prerequisites\nStart the server (`npm start` in `server/`); you should see `Database connected: ...`. Player money moves additionally require `sweepstakes-backend` running at the tenant's `platformUrl`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Signs every request with the agent-platform HMAC scheme.",
          "// Runs before any folder/request script, so negative tests can override it.",
          "const operatorId = pm.collectionVariables.get('operatorId');",
          "const apiKey = pm.collectionVariables.get('apiKey');",
          "const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get('signingSecret');",
          "",
          "// Sign the EXACT bytes that will be sent (resolve {{vars}} first).",
          "let rawBody = '';",
          "if (pm.request.body && pm.request.body.mode === 'raw' && pm.request.body.raw) {",
          "  rawBody = pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.body.raw.toString());",
          "}",
          "",
          "const ts = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000).toString();",
          "const signature = CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(ts + '.' + rawBody, secret).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
          "",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'x-operator-id', value: operatorId });",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'x-api-key', value: apiKey });",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'x-timestamp', value: ts });",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'x-signature', value: signature });"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4100",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "operatorId",
      "value": "demo-operator",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "demo-api-key",
      "type": "secret"
    },
    {
      "key": "signingSecret",
      "value": "demo-signing-secret",
      "type": "secret"
    },
    {
      "key": "managerUsername",
      "value": "mgr1",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "createKey",
      "value": "k-mgr1",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "creditKey",
      "value": "k-credit1",
      "type": "default"
    },
    {
      "key": "withdrawKey",
      "value": "k-wd1",
      "type": "default"
